{"revision_id":100,"metadata":{"report_numbers":[{"value":"DPNU-7-78"}],"publication_info":[{"year":1978,"artid":"479","page_start":"479","journal_title":"Annals Phys.","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214855"},"journal_volume":"114"}],"citation_count_without_self_citations":43,"citation_count":43,"dois":[{"value":"10.1016/0003-4916(78)90279-8"}],"titles":[{"title":"Quantum Mechanics of Nonconservative Systems"},{"title":"QUANTUM MECHANICS OF NONCONSERVATIVE SYSTEMS"}],"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","authors":[{"uuid":"29e434ae-1acd-4d84-846c-281b4101ae67","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/2237716"},"full_name":"Yasue, Kunio","affiliations":[{"value":"Nagoya U.","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/903041"}}],"signature_block":"YASk"}],"curated":true,"texkeys":["Yasue:1978bx"],"citeable":true,"refereed":true,"abstracts":[{"value":"The quantum theoretic formulation of open dynamical systems interacting with chaotic thermal environments is investigated. Nelson's stochastic quantization procedure is adopted to derive the Schrödinger-Langevin equation which describes the irreversible behavior of an open system. Then, taking a classical limit of the Schrödinger-Langev in equation, we obtain the Hamilton-Jacobi equation for classical irreversible dynamics. The asymptotic form of the Hamilton-Jacobi equation and Schröndinger's quantization procedure give us a nonlinear Schrödinger equation which describes quantum theoretic asymptote of the open system. For the purpose of analyzing quantum-mechanical irreversible behaviors of open many-body systems a field theoretic treatment of the Schrödinger-Langevin equation is presented. As an application of the method to a physical system the thermal decay of the ac Josephson current near the critical temperature is investigated.","source":"Elsevier"}],"references":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3608"},"referen